I see the problem! When `fgetc` returns EOF, I'm not breaking out of the loop properly. The issue is that when we hit EOF without reading any characters (empty input), we return an empty string and then keep looping forever because `read_line` keeps returning a buffer with length 0.

The fix: when we get EOF on the first character (no data read), we should return NULL to signal end of file:
